   {
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "id": "9c0de904",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "# Comprehensive Inference Benchmarking\n",
     "\n",
     "This notebook provides a unified benchmark of various convolutional neural network (CNN) architectures, including standard baselines and retrained weights. We evaluate the trade-off between:\n",
     "\n",
     "* **Accuracy**: Performance on validation datasets.\n",
     "* **Computational Cost**: Inference speed (wall clock time) and model complexity (total parameters).\n",
     "* **Masking Impact**: The effect of partial image masking (`do_mask`) on performance across different architectures.\n",
     "\n",
     "We compare three main categories of models:\n",
    "1. **Baseline ResNets**: Standard pre-trained architectures (ResNet18, 50, 101).\n",
    "2. **ConvNeXt family**: Scaling analysis across Tiny, Small, Base, and Large variants.\n",
    "3. **Retrained Models**: Models that have been specifically retrained on masked/bbox data (from script 21)."
     ]
    }
   ],
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": 1,
    "id": "efdb6e14-6ce3-481d-9afc-61b1cfee1168",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "import retinoto_py as fovea\n",
     "args = fovea.Params(do_fovea=False, do_augment=False, verbose=False)\n",
     "args"
    ]
   },
   {
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "id": "d906f00e",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "# Benchmarking Loop\n",
     "\n",
     "We iterate over all supported architectures, datasets, and masking configurations. For each combination, we attempt to load retrained weights from the cache; if none are available, we fall back to the standard pre-trained baseline."
    ]
   },
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": 3,
    "id": "c4e5bc5b",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "json_filename = args.data_cache / '13_unified_model_comparison.json'\n",
     "\n",
     "if json_filename.exists():\n",
     "    results = fovea.pd.read_json(json_filename)\n",
     "else:\n",
     "    all_results = []\n",
     "    # Combine all architecture lists into one master list for benchmarking\n",
     "    all_architectures = fovea.params.all_rn_model_names + fovea.params.all_cn_model_names\n",
     "    \n",
     "    for do_mask in [True, False]:\n",
     "        for dataset in fovea.params.all_datasets:\n",
     "            # Setup loader once per configuration\n",
     "            args_bench = fovea.Params(do_mask=do_mask, do_fovea=False, do_augment=False)\n",
     "            val_loader = fovea.get_val_loader(args_bench, dataset)\n",
     "            \n",
     "            for model_name in all_architectures:\n",
     "                args_bench.model_name = model_name\n",
     "                \n",
     "                # Check if a retrained version of the model exists for this dataset (from script 21)\n",
     "                retrained_filename = args.data_cache / f'21_model_name={model_name}_dataset={dataset}.pth'\n",
     "                \n",
     "                if retrained_filename.exists():\n",
     "                    # Use retrained weights\n",
     "                    model = fovea.load_model(args_bench, model_filename=retrained_filename)\n",
     "                    weight_type = 'retrained'\n",
     "                else:\n",
     "                    # Fallback to baseline pre-trained weights\n",
     "                    model = fovea.load_model(args_bench)\n",
     "                    weight_type = 'baseline'\n",
     "                \n",
     "                param_stats = fovea.count_parameters(model)\n",
     "                total_layers = fovea.count_layers(model)\n",
     "                \n",
     "                tic = fovea.time.time()\n",
     "                accuracy = fovea.get_validation_accuracy(\n",
     "                    args_bench, model, val_loader, \n",
     "                    f\"Model {model_name} ({weight_type})\\t dataset: {dataset}\\t(do_mask={do_mask})\"\n",
     "                )\n",
     "                toc = fovea.time.time()\n",
     "                \n",
     "                all_results.append({\n",
     "                    'model_name': model_name,\n",
     "                    'weight_type': weight_type,\n",
     "                    'do_mask': do_mask,\n",
     "                    'dataset': dataset,\n",
     "                    'accuracy': accuracy,\n",
     "                    'wall_clock_time': (toc-tic)/len(val_loader.dataset),\n",
     "                    'total_parameters': param_stats['total_parameters'],\n",
     "                    'trainable_parameters': param_stats['trainable_parameters'],\n",
     "                    'total_layers': total_layers\n",
     "                })\n",
     "    \n",
     "    results = fovea.pd.DataFrame(all_results)\n",
     "    results.to_json(json_filename, orient='records', indent=2)\n"
    ]
   },
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": 4,
    "id": "f7fe5053",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "# Review the aggregated performance metrics\n",
     "results.T"
    ]
   },
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
    "execution_count": 5,
    "id": "bf592ebb",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "# Visualize the results using a unified comparison plot\n",
     "fig, axes = fovea.plot_model_comparison(\n",
     "    results,\n",
     "    all_architectures := (fovea.params.all_rn_model_names + fovea.params.all_cn_model_names),\n",
     "    fovea.params.all_datasets,\n",
     "    do_masks=[True, False],\n",
     "    figures_folder=args.figures_folder,\n",
     "    save_name='13_unified_model_comparison',\n",
     "    exts=['svg', 'pdf']\n",
     ")\n",
     "fovea.plt.show()"
    ]
   }
  ],
